# src/apps/daemon/internal/runtime/safety

## Purpose
Canonical safety-policy owner shared by HTTP, mobile, and runtime sidecars; one policy truth across adapters.

## Architectural role
- Daemon dependency band: `runtime` (rank 4; lower rank = deeper implementation).
- Cross-band imports may point only to a lower rank. Same-band imports are allowed when they remain within one architectural layer.

## Contents
- Direct files (2): `safety.go`, `safety_test.go`

## Interfaces and dependencies
- Go package: `safety`.
- Notable exported surface: `DefaultSettings`, `GetGovernor`, `Governor`, `NewGovernor`, `Settings`.
- Daemon-local dependencies: none.
- Direct daemon callers: `internal/adapters/api`, `internal/adapters/mobilebind`.

## Invariants
- HTTP, mobile, and runtime callers consult the same safety policy state.
- `runtime` code must not import a higher-rank daemon band.

## Navigation
- Read this file first, then direct child `.context` files before editing a deeper folder.
- Update this context when ownership, supported interfaces, or child-folder meaning changes; do not use it as a changelog.
